.SS CVE\-2021\-36942
Microsoft Windows, added 2021\-11\-03, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Microsoft Windows Local Security Authority (LSA) Spoofing Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft Windows Local Security Authority (LSA) contains a spoofing vulnerability allowing an unauthenticated attacker to call a method on the LSARPC interface and coerce the domain controller to authenticate against another server using NTLM.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2021\-11\-17.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2021\-36942
.SS CVE\-2026\-116779
SignalWire FreeSwitch, added 2026\-11\-09.
.PP
SignalWire FreeSwitch Code Injection Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
SignalWire FreeSwitch contains a code injection vulnerability that permits configuration and credential disclosure, arbitrary call control, and command execution.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-11\-12.
.PP
